# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  theourgia_wm_simsess.la — the headless tiling WM with LogosSession behind
#  its lock screen, on the path the live WM takes.
#
#  theourgia_wm_sim.la runs the WM headless with SIM_SESS, a stand-in session
#  layer. This entry is the same run (SIM_RUN, imported from it) with the
#  lock screen the live WM has (theourgia_wm_live.la), built by the same
#  code, logos_realsess.la's REAL_LOCK: the users directory through
#  wm_livestart.la's USERS_KIT (made 0700 when missing; a first run when
#  DIR/users does not exist), LogosSession's login, lock, unlock and adduser
#  over it (logossession.la, on CRYPT_FAST, logossec.la and AletheiaFS), and
#  lk_firstuser.la's app. The WM starts LOCKED: at the first-run screen on a
#  first run, at the login screen otherwise. So making the first user runs
#  LogosSession's adduser, unlocking the screen stretches the passphrase with
#  PBKDF2, derives the user's Γ-seal and opens the user's store, and locking
#  drops every key derived from it.
#
#  CONFIGURATION: wm_sim.cfg as for theourgia_wm_sim.la, and users=DIR is
#  required: DIR is LogosSession's root (DIR/users/<name>, DIR/home/<name>),
#  read as the live WM reads the first line of logos_wm.users. A DIR that is
#  a regular file, or whose parent is missing, stops the run before anything
#  is drawn.
#
#  It is a separate entry, not an option of theourgia_wm_sim.la, so that the
#  WM gates which do not need the session layer do not compile it.
#  gate_wm_simsess.sh drives it.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

import("theourgia_wm_sim.la")
import("logos_realsess.la")

glyph MAIN = SIM_RUN(la users. str_eq(users)("")
  (la _. error("wm_simsess: wm_sim.cfg needs users=DIR, the directory of LogosSession's users"))
  (la _. SIM_UI(REAL_LOCK(users)))("!"))
